1
00:00:01,640 --> 00:00:03,600
Please insert coins.

2
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:11,400
Well, time to slowly get
crushed into oblivion.

3
00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:17,820
Hold up!

4
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:22,648
It seems the nefarious Netherlord can't
see me, which only changes everything.

5
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:25,157
There we go.

6
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:28,300
Next up, I'll cleverly spend
the points I have left.

7
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:31,620
Guess who's good as new?

8
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:42,580
Small call.

9
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:45,057
These babies are used in dioramas,

10
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:49,140
and according to my research, they're
the smallest vending machines.

11
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:00,720
Boxxo is back!

12
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:03,257
Hopefully the nether dork
thinks I kicked the bucket,

13
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:06,222
but I'd better camouflage
myself just to be safe.

14
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:14,680
What in the heck?

15
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:17,428
Why'd he make a supersized
summoning circle?

16
00:01:22,020 --> 00:01:23,040
Red alert!

17
00:01:23,320 --> 00:01:25,849
That freak combined
all the Stratum bosses!

18
00:01:26,180 --> 00:01:29,592
Ruh-roh, that means this mad
monster's packing peak power!

19
00:01:34,980 --> 00:01:38,509
It's only a matter of time until
this whole place collapses!

20
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:46,780
Behold, as I entomb that foolish demon
lord and assert control over my own domain!

21
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:52,464
And that's how I wound up living
underground for four whole days.

22
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:55,757
I bunkered up with telekinesis
and concrete blocks,

23
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:57,899
plus flowers for a splash of color.

24
00:01:58,240 --> 00:02:01,760
It sure is lonesome being
buried alive, but it's fine.

25
00:02:02,020 --> 00:02:04,667
I know Lamas will give
it her all to find me.

26
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:08,460
Oh Lamas, you've come such a long way.

27
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:09,597
When we met,

28
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:13,357
other hunters thought you were useless and
you'd even been abandoned by your team.

29
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:16,146
I'm sure that must have
hurt like the dickens.

30
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:18,817
But check out your glow up.

31
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:22,777
Now you're an able hunter and a household
name in the clear flow lake stratum.

32
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:25,177
I've literally had your
back this whole time.

33
00:02:25,260 --> 00:02:28,084
So just thinking about
it gets me all verklempt.

34
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:30,880
She told me we could
stay together forever.

35
00:02:31,820 --> 00:02:33,217
Once this little mess is settled.

36
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:37,829
I have no doubt she'll help me conquer
another dungeon to become human again.

37
00:02:38,260 --> 00:02:40,437
Seems the rest of the gang
wants to tag along too.

38
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:41,820
Road trip baby.

39
00:02:42,380 --> 00:02:46,517
As long as I can keep adventuring with
this rowdy yet lovable band of misfits,

40
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:47,953
I've got no complaints.

41
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:50,560
Welp, time for the yuge.

42
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:53,757
I'll show these meanies what
vending machines are made of.

43
00:02:53,840 --> 00:03:05,423
Come over there!

44
00:03:05,506 --> 00:03:06,336
Fox Show!

45
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:19,637
On the outside, I'm just a big metal box,
but inside, I've still got a human soul!

46
00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:21,177
In this new world of wonders,

47
00:03:21,260 --> 00:03:24,757
I travel to and fro on the back
of my super strong partner, Lamas!

48
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:26,840
The name's Boxxo! Hello there!

49
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:28,680
That means yes, by the way!

50
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:45,157
Love it, to eat, to bring it to you.

51
00:03:56,460 --> 00:04:02,040
Don't see a crash, baby,
I'm so sure I'm getting it.

52
00:04:03,220 --> 00:04:05,660
I'm getting out of this universe,

53
00:04:05,840 --> 00:04:11,800
you will get it.

54
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,420
That voice.

55
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:04,900
It's Lawless, hello there.

56
00:05:13,500 --> 00:05:15,277
Phew, glad you're not squished.

57
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:16,637
Good to have you back.

58
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:18,717
Everyone's feeling worried sick about you.

59
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:21,153
We should have known you'd be just fine.

60
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:26,400
I missed you so much.

61
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:27,937
You're not broken, are you?

62
00:05:28,020 --> 00:05:29,200
Or scratched up?

63
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:30,877
I was so...

64
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:33,017
Honestly, you're lucky to be in one piece.

65
00:05:33,100 --> 00:05:35,157
But you don't always have
to push your luck, you know.

66
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:36,070
Yes.

67
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:38,220
We finally made it.

68
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:39,657
How's it going, Boxel?

69
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:42,577
Is it too soon to ask you
to dish out some snacks?

70
00:05:42,660 --> 00:05:44,980
Boxo's been dug out, can you dig it?

71
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:47,997
I always knew you'd make
it out of this, okay, pal.

72
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:50,140
Beyond a shadow of a doubt.

73
00:05:51,340 --> 00:05:54,337
Your humor leaves a lot to
be desired, Director Dog.

74
00:05:54,420 --> 00:05:56,420
Hey, Boxo, it's good to see you.

75
00:05:57,060 --> 00:05:59,001
The directors are safe and sound.

76
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:00,748
But wait, where's the bear?

77
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:03,460
Well, it's every when.

78
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:05,800
Oh, all of our friends are safe.

79
00:06:05,980 --> 00:06:07,877
Director Bear and the others are busy.

80
00:06:07,960 --> 00:06:09,417
They're pursuing the monster horde.

81
00:06:09,500 --> 00:06:12,940
Knowing my buddies are okay
is a huge load off my ram.

82
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:14,900
Now, time to get vending.

83
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:20,757
Seeing as how the town was destroyed,
there aren't a ton of food options.

84
00:06:20,840 --> 00:06:24,140
This calls for a lavish
feast. Hello there.

85
00:06:24,660 --> 00:06:27,997
There's plenty to go around, so
just wait your turn, everyone.

86
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:29,640
And remember, be fair.

87
00:06:29,820 --> 00:06:33,157
Children and old people go first,
so don't try to cut the line.

88
00:06:33,240 --> 00:06:34,181
Hello, everyone.

89
00:06:34,320 --> 00:06:35,317
Want some sweet food?

90
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:38,576
Trust me, you're gonna flip
when you taste this stuff.

91
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:46,529
In the end, I doled out packaged prezzies
until the wee hours of the morning.

92
00:06:47,420 --> 00:06:50,949
Pretty sure we've got enough
Boxxo food to last a while now.

93
00:06:51,100 --> 00:06:52,300
A job well done.

94
00:06:52,560 --> 00:06:56,678
Since they're not going to starve,
we can go catch up with the others.

95
00:06:57,540 --> 00:07:01,246
I'm told Captain Carriol's family
went after the monster horde.

96
00:07:01,740 --> 00:07:03,137
Meanwhile, Director Bear,

97
00:07:03,220 --> 00:07:04,050
the guards,

98
00:07:04,133 --> 00:07:08,528
Heavy, and Mishuel are in a mad dash to
beat the beasts to the fortified city.

99
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:12,742
You better make sure you take a
little break if you need to, Boxo.

100
00:07:13,960 --> 00:07:14,790
I agree.

101
00:07:15,140 --> 00:07:16,100
Just relax.

102
00:07:16,580 --> 00:07:18,480
Live a little, Boxo. Ah!

103
00:07:19,760 --> 00:07:21,377
Take your hands to yourself!

104
00:07:21,460 --> 00:07:22,777
We know you've been through a lot,

105
00:07:22,860 --> 00:07:25,337
so it's probably a good idea
to take it easy for a bit.

106
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:26,560
Oh, thank you.

107
00:07:27,180 --> 00:07:28,240
They need to rest.

108
00:07:28,420 --> 00:07:30,177
Those four stayed up all night with me.

109
00:07:30,260 --> 00:07:32,417
But I won't stop till the job is done.

110
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:34,980
You never change, do you, kiddo? Huh?

111
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:50,358
Getting so old you wake up
early does have its perks.

112
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:53,186
My skin's not porcine,
but aging's not so bad.

113
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:54,675
Collagen's overrated.

114
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:59,260
The senior squad came equipped.

115
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:00,977
He thinks they want to tag along.

116
00:08:01,060 --> 00:08:02,620
Count me in too, big boy.

117
00:08:03,020 --> 00:08:04,437
I'm getting fired up.

118
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:07,167
Guess they're coming
along for the ride, too.

119
00:08:07,500 --> 00:08:09,557
Oh, I hate getting up early.

120
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:11,237
You sound like a spoiled brat.

121
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:14,017
Splash some water on your face
and pull yourself together, boy.

122
00:08:14,100 --> 00:08:15,040
I don't wanna.

123
00:08:15,580 --> 00:08:17,109
Our team will remain here.

124
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:19,740
We'll work on rebuilding the town. Nice!

125
00:08:19,980 --> 00:08:21,897
Now I don't have to
worry about this place.

126
00:08:21,980 --> 00:08:24,098
I know I'm leaving it in good hands.

127
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:28,437
Why do men always sneak
away in the morning?

128
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:29,840
We'll miss you, Boxo.

129
00:08:30,220 --> 00:08:32,280
Lamy, please be careful out there.

130
00:08:32,420 --> 00:08:33,917
Be sure to give them help for us.

131
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,160
Thank you. Steak you.

132
00:08:36,740 --> 00:08:39,400
Well, is everyone ready
to get going? Yeah!

133
00:08:44,980 --> 00:08:48,392
Isn't it a tad silly to be
hiding behind a tree like that?

134
00:08:50,020 --> 00:08:51,060
Oh, goodness.

135
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:53,774
I didn't think you'd be able to see me.

136
00:08:56,320 --> 00:08:58,217
Pleased to make your acquaintance.

137
00:08:58,300 --> 00:09:02,594
And I deeply apologize for all the
trouble my naughty son has caused you.

138
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:05,915
Who the heck are you?

139
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,377
And who's this alleged
son you're talking about?

140
00:09:08,460 --> 00:09:09,720
Oh, how spicy.

141
00:09:10,180 --> 00:09:11,298
Ribby's pernicious.

142
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:13,421
He's my little rascal, after all.

143
00:09:14,100 --> 00:09:17,677
Uh, lady, not to be mean, but is
Ribby in the room with us right now?

144
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:20,697
When he was a child, he was
so quiet and mild-mannered.

145
00:09:20,780 --> 00:09:24,457
Where do you suppose I went wrong
for him to turn out the way he did?

146
00:09:24,540 --> 00:09:26,720
I almost forgot, little Ribby.

147
00:09:26,880 --> 00:09:29,137
I hear he goes by a
different name these days.

148
00:09:29,220 --> 00:09:33,240
I think it was, oh, now I
remember, the Netherlord.

149
00:09:35,720 --> 00:09:37,500
The Nether Mama showed up?

150
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:39,012
Talk about a plot twist.

151
00:09:46,540 --> 00:09:48,220
I know kids like to rebel,

152
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:50,337
but I still can't believe he experimented

153
00:09:50,420 --> 00:09:53,008
on his own mother to
get that skeleton body.

154
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:58,037
As if that weren't bad enough,
he also won't let me die.

155
00:09:58,120 --> 00:09:59,557
How could he be so cruel?

156
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:04,440
He used his own mother as a test
subject for his twisted dark art!

157
00:10:05,860 --> 00:10:07,040
Damn, Netherlord!

158
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:11,025
I knew you were mega-scum, but
this is full-on psycho territory!

159
00:10:11,400 --> 00:10:15,217
Of course, a mother's love is eternal,
so I forgive him for everything!

160
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:17,497
Now I'm the Thumb
General and I strike down

161
00:10:17,580 --> 00:10:20,051
anyone who dares to stand in my son's way!

162
00:10:20,400 --> 00:10:21,780
I'm a good mother!

163
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:25,889
Alright, so just to be clear,
are you gonna try and kill us?

164
00:10:26,620 --> 00:10:28,120
Of course I am!

165
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:31,438
A mother's love is nothing
if it's not unconditional!

166
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:35,457
That's a lovely maternal
sentiment on paper,

167
00:10:35,540 --> 00:10:37,952
but it doesn't entail aiding mass murder!

168
00:10:38,460 --> 00:10:41,097
Seems to me you're a
sorry excuse for a mother.

169
00:10:41,180 --> 00:10:45,357
When a child is misbehaving, it's a
mother's duty to smack some sense into us.

170
00:10:45,440 --> 00:10:49,377
The situation you just described isn't
a mother's love, it's indulgence!

171
00:10:49,460 --> 00:10:50,580
Don't say that!

172
00:10:50,760 --> 00:10:53,037
How dare you condemn me when
I've given him everything!

173
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:56,297
Don't you fool see that I'm
the best mother there ever was?

174
00:10:56,380 --> 00:10:59,498
Everyone in the world except
my ribby and me can die!

175
00:11:00,060 --> 00:11:02,472
The apples didn't fall far from the tree.

176
00:11:02,560 --> 00:11:05,837
There's clearly no point trying
to reason with the thumb, General.

177
00:11:05,920 --> 00:11:08,685
Anyone who isn't fighting,
follow me to safety!

178
00:11:14,880 --> 00:11:16,560
It's time to die!

179
00:11:24,740 --> 00:11:27,446
Did you think we'd let
you get away with this?

180
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:33,360
You cowards are ganging up on me.

181
00:11:33,500 --> 00:11:34,960
It's inexcusable.

182
00:11:35,860 --> 00:11:37,600
John, it's feeding time.

183
00:11:39,680 --> 00:11:42,657
That looks like the summoning
circle the Netherlord used.

184
00:11:42,740 --> 00:11:44,681
Pretty clear where this is going.

185
00:11:45,100 --> 00:11:49,571
I've got a real bad feeling about that
summoning circle, so watch your back.

186
00:11:49,660 --> 00:11:50,700
Come on, Gramps.

187
00:11:50,820 --> 00:11:52,337
Could it really be that bad?

188
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:53,250
It could.

189
00:11:53,333 --> 00:11:55,180
That mana is downright alien.

190
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:57,940
It may be a monster from another world.

191
00:11:58,220 --> 00:11:59,640
Holy Isekai!

192
00:12:00,780 --> 00:12:03,074
What's that weird monster-shaped thing?

193
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:06,317
I've seen more than my fair
share of monsters here.

194
00:12:06,400 --> 00:12:08,047
But that thing's ridiculous!

195
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:12,980
Boxxo! Boxxo! Boxxo!

196
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:24,510
Oh, wow.

197
00:12:27,340 --> 00:12:29,520
You can leave this nasty fella to us.

198
00:12:29,740 --> 00:12:31,997
We're all itching to get in on the action.

199
00:12:32,080 --> 00:12:35,897
Once you get as old as we are, you're
too short on time to bother with fear.

200
00:12:35,980 --> 00:12:39,097
I don't know, the two of you still
find ways to scare me occasionally.

201
00:12:39,180 --> 00:12:41,840
It does get intense when
you two are arguing.

202
00:12:42,020 --> 00:12:43,957
Oh, yeah, now I'm doubly fired up.

203
00:12:44,040 --> 00:12:46,597
The forces of justice
fighting back against evil?

204
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:48,915
Yeah, this is what dreams are made of!

205
00:12:58,220 --> 00:12:59,050
Simmer down.

206
00:13:00,560 --> 00:13:02,477
Oh, things are getting hot in here.

207
00:13:02,560 --> 00:13:06,384
Looks like these buggies like to
explode whenever you blast them.

208
00:13:11,140 --> 00:13:12,300
Hey, what the hey?

209
00:13:12,620 --> 00:13:15,637
If this becomes a war of attrition,
stamina could be a real problem.

210
00:13:15,720 --> 00:13:20,480
If only I could distract our opponent
with some kind of elaborate display wait,

211
00:13:20,720 --> 00:13:22,485
I'm a freaking vending machine

212
00:13:45,020 --> 00:13:47,057
Fireworks are always something special,

213
00:13:47,140 --> 00:13:49,497
but there's nothing like
your very first time.

214
00:13:49,580 --> 00:13:50,756
There's the big bug.

215
00:13:50,980 --> 00:13:54,497
It's not really advancing, but it's
also facing away from the fireworks.

216
00:13:54,580 --> 00:13:55,837
Which means...

217
00:13:55,920 --> 00:13:57,500
My hunch was right.

218
00:13:57,720 --> 00:14:01,367
The thumb general is the one
pulling its gross little strings.

219
00:14:02,420 --> 00:14:05,140
Simply gorgeous. Lock it. Huh?

220
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:06,986
Did you need something, Boxo?

221
00:14:09,560 --> 00:14:10,390
Yup.

222
00:14:10,473 --> 00:14:11,303
Now that I'm ranked three,

223
00:14:11,386 --> 00:14:14,829
I can spawn concrete blocks
nearby instead of just under me.

224
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:16,997
So, um, you want me to throw these?

225
00:14:17,080 --> 00:14:17,910
Hello there.

226
00:14:17,993 --> 00:14:19,960
At the Thumb General. Yes.

227
00:14:20,580 --> 00:14:21,880
Okay, you got it.

228
00:14:28,620 --> 00:14:29,450
Success!

229
00:14:29,900 --> 00:14:33,017
I turned into a cardboard vending
machine just before she threw it.

230
00:14:33,100 --> 00:14:34,917
I won't get anywhere
near the Thumb General.

231
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:35,830
No big.

232
00:14:35,913 --> 00:14:38,228
I factored Lamas' bad
aim into the equation.

233
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:43,420
What the? It's Boxxo!

234
00:14:52,940 --> 00:14:54,340
They're so beautiful.

235
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:57,525
I wish I could watch them
with my little ribby.

236
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:08,177
Our defeat of the Thumb General
calls for a victory dance.

237
00:15:08,260 --> 00:15:11,117
But that would mean crashing
and burning, so maybe not.

238
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:13,141
Luckily, I have an exit strategy.

239
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:22,020
I should be in the clear now. Huh?

240
00:15:22,340 --> 00:15:24,340
What's this weird Field feeling?

241
00:15:25,260 --> 00:15:27,380
Boxo, you did something crazy again.

242
00:15:28,580 --> 00:15:29,410
Sorry.

243
00:15:29,660 --> 00:15:32,897
Don't think I'm going to let you off
the hook just because you're adorable.

244
00:15:32,980 --> 00:15:34,040
Oh, the bug.

245
00:15:34,240 --> 00:15:35,711
Is it vanquished or what?

246
00:15:39,660 --> 00:15:42,117
Without its summoner
binding it to this world,

247
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:44,237
that beast went back from whence it came.

248
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:45,908
Textbook monster summoning.

249
00:15:46,560 --> 00:15:50,797
That takes care of, well, the side
story, which still leaves the main plot.

250
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:53,409
We gotta hurry and
catch up to our friends!

251
00:15:57,380 --> 00:15:58,210
Boom!

252
00:15:58,293 --> 00:16:00,157
The mythical vehicle vending machine,

253
00:16:00,240 --> 00:16:02,497
famous amongst fellow
vending machine enthusiasts.

254
00:16:02,580 --> 00:16:06,677
When the uninitiated behold its glory,
they often mistake it for a building.

255
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:09,400
Boxo, are you gonna give us another A-car?

256
00:16:10,020 --> 00:16:12,217
Our party's gotten pretty bloated,

257
00:16:12,300 --> 00:16:14,777
and the ground's not flat
like the everlasting stratum.

258
00:16:14,860 --> 00:16:17,684
I've got to take the bumpy
terrain into account.

259
00:16:17,900 --> 00:16:18,730
Hmm.

260
00:16:18,860 --> 00:16:19,797
Which means...

261
00:16:19,880 --> 00:16:21,000
A pick-up truck!

262
00:16:26,880 --> 00:16:29,527
That A-car looks different
from the last one.

263
00:16:29,620 --> 00:16:30,637
Yeah, you're right.

264
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:33,117
It's definitely a lot
bigger than our old one.

265
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:34,480
It's so cool!

266
00:16:34,780 --> 00:16:35,820
We like it!

267
00:16:38,940 --> 00:16:43,597
A lot of these roads are uneven, so I know
dispensing a truck was the right call.

268
00:16:43,680 --> 00:16:45,937
There's plenty of room
even with yours truly.

269
00:16:46,020 --> 00:16:49,549
Since it's a foreign build, the
standard size is still huge.

270
00:16:49,760 --> 00:16:51,957
I'm really starting to
like driving this thing.

271
00:16:52,040 --> 00:16:53,697
I'm going to go a little faster.

272
00:16:53,780 --> 00:16:56,956
It's been a pleasant drive,
but it's almost lunchtime.

273
00:16:57,080 --> 00:16:59,727
I wonder what I should
feed my friends today.

274
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:02,100
Ooh, I know just the thing.

275
00:17:07,780 --> 00:17:10,360
My pals are in for a tasty treat.

276
00:17:10,960 --> 00:17:11,790
Blammo!

277
00:17:11,873 --> 00:17:15,137
A pizza vending machine baked to
order with all the right topics.

278
00:17:15,220 --> 00:17:17,161
It's an authentic Italiano model.

279
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:19,480
Whatever it is looks good.

280
00:17:21,460 --> 00:17:22,342
It's delicious.

281
00:17:22,820 --> 00:17:24,637
Whoa, what is this crazy stuff?

282
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:26,837
You pull it apart and it gets so stretchy.

283
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:28,100
It was such a hit.

284
00:17:28,300 --> 00:17:29,817
They ate it all in record time.

285
00:17:29,900 --> 00:17:30,877
Don't hold out on us.

286
00:17:30,960 --> 00:17:32,577
Pop out the good stuff already.

287
00:17:32,660 --> 00:17:34,917
Hmm, someone's addicted, but I only vend.

288
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:35,830
I don't judge.

289
00:17:35,913 --> 00:17:39,211
I'm so happy everyone loves my
hot and ready pizza so much.

290
00:17:40,320 --> 00:17:41,150
Weird.

291
00:17:41,233 --> 00:17:42,337
They barely touched their zah.

292
00:17:42,420 --> 00:17:43,250
Oh, snap!

293
00:17:43,340 --> 00:17:46,693
It must be too heavy for their
ancient tummies to handle.

294
00:17:49,420 --> 00:17:50,250
Thank you.

295
00:17:50,420 --> 00:17:52,657
It's kind of you to
fuss over us like that.

296
00:17:52,740 --> 00:17:55,617
The last thing was interesting,
but just a little too rich.

297
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:57,197
Thanks for thinking of us.

298
00:17:57,280 --> 00:18:00,620
Though I hate to waste
perfectly good food. No worries.

299
00:18:01,140 --> 00:18:02,977
Shui, those are all
yours if you want them.

300
00:18:03,060 --> 00:18:05,677
If I'm dreaming, you'll be here
till I'm done eating, okay?

301
00:18:05,760 --> 00:18:08,397
Oh, Shui, your stomach's
as bottomless as ever.

302
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:09,640
Just to be safe,

303
00:18:09,820 --> 00:18:14,349
I'll load her up on lots of burgers and
fried chicken before we hit the road.

304
00:18:16,260 --> 00:18:19,142
Hey, Boxel, can I have
one of those fizzy drinks?

305
00:18:20,540 --> 00:18:21,370
Now what?

306
00:18:21,453 --> 00:18:23,917
We need to devise a plan
to stop the Netherlord.

307
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:26,737
His powers are a pain in the
rear, but with all these points,

308
00:18:26,820 --> 00:18:29,297
I wonder if I could use
my barrier to blow...

309
00:18:29,380 --> 00:18:33,380
Hey, my tummy's feeling a little
angry, so how about a little snack?

310
00:18:33,900 --> 00:18:36,597
I'll just wait to attack
until his tummy's angry.

311
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:38,440
No, focus! Let's think.

312
00:18:38,620 --> 00:18:41,757
Of the Finger Generals, I've defeated
the thumb and the middle fingy.

313
00:18:41,840 --> 00:18:44,380
Ring finger General
Solreen switched sides.

314
00:18:44,600 --> 00:18:45,680
That just leaves.

315
00:18:45,960 --> 00:18:48,360
Boxo, I'm still starving over here!

316
00:18:49,840 --> 00:18:53,320
The diabetes-inducing
sweetbread general... Dadnobbit!

317
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:55,637
I mean, the last two
generals will be tough.

318
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:59,037
The pinky general got away, and there's
no telling where the forefinger...

319
00:18:59,120 --> 00:19:02,857
I need something really sweet to help
wash down all that tasty food now.

320
00:19:02,940 --> 00:19:03,770
Right.

321
00:19:03,853 --> 00:19:05,217
Then there's the dreaded juice general.

322
00:19:05,300 --> 00:19:07,440
Will you stop distracting me, Shwee?

323
00:19:07,540 --> 00:19:10,817
I am this close to letting Hulemy
dissect your stomach for science.

324
00:19:10,900 --> 00:19:12,841
I'm not getting any less thirsty.

325
00:19:13,500 --> 00:19:16,117
Shwee's had enough sugar
to kill a grown elephant,

326
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:18,376
so let's try a zero-calorie beverage.

327
00:19:19,220 --> 00:19:20,180
What is this?

328
00:19:20,340 --> 00:19:22,717
There's something off
about the sweetness of it.

329
00:19:22,800 --> 00:19:24,212
It tastes okay, I guess.

330
00:19:24,740 --> 00:19:28,297
She not only eats a lot, but it seems
her sense of taste is also shockingly?

331
00:19:28,380 --> 00:19:29,760
and annoyingly refined.

332
00:19:30,180 --> 00:19:33,121
You're not thinking something
rude, are you, Boxo?

333
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:34,500
Gaining what?

334
00:19:35,300 --> 00:19:36,497
Someone's gaining weight?

335
00:19:36,580 --> 00:19:37,410
Me?

336
00:19:37,493 --> 00:19:38,357
Is that what you're saying?

337
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:40,577
I'm in the middle of
a bulking phase, dude.

338
00:19:40,660 --> 00:19:41,600
Fat Boxxo.

339
00:19:41,740 --> 00:19:43,777
It's against the law to
talk about a girl's weight.

340
00:19:43,860 --> 00:19:44,690
Got it?

341
00:19:44,773 --> 00:19:45,603
Hello there.

342
00:19:46,320 --> 00:19:48,140
The road trip went smoothly.

343
00:19:48,360 --> 00:19:51,137
No accidents or illegal
fat comments to speak of.

344
00:19:51,220 --> 00:19:52,577
It only took us a few days.

345
00:19:52,660 --> 00:19:54,820
This contraption sure is handy.

346
00:19:55,040 --> 00:19:58,216
I can see things in the
far-off distance clear as day.

347
00:19:58,500 --> 00:20:01,206
Don't forget to revel
in the glory of vending.

348
00:20:02,220 --> 00:20:03,440
Oh, dear. Gramps!

349
00:20:03,680 --> 00:20:04,797
No need to shout.

350
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:06,820
I'm right behind you. Up ahead.

351
00:20:06,980 --> 00:20:09,417
There's a standoff against
a horde of monsters.

352
00:20:09,500 --> 00:20:10,330
Are you sure?

353
00:20:10,413 --> 00:20:11,615
Let me have a gander.

354
00:20:12,480 --> 00:20:13,400
It's serious.

355
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:15,780
I'm not loving their odds.

356
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:17,497
The poor saps are outnumbered.

357
00:20:17,580 --> 00:20:20,417
If they're way out here, does
that mean what I think it does?

358
00:20:20,500 --> 00:20:23,676
Hulemy, head right and make
this thing go even faster.

359
00:20:24,040 --> 00:20:24,870
Got it.

360
00:20:24,953 --> 00:20:25,975
It'll be my pleasure.

361
00:20:28,620 --> 00:20:30,297
This is all kinds of bad.

362
00:20:30,380 --> 00:20:32,037
They're completely surrounded.

363
00:20:32,120 --> 00:20:33,957
With them packed so tightly together,

364
00:20:34,040 --> 00:20:36,137
it would be too dangerous
to try a magic strike.

365
00:20:36,220 --> 00:20:38,057
Pretty sure we'd try to set it to.

366
00:20:38,140 --> 00:20:41,197
Oh, Shimei Lion Director Scorching
can't push the wind button?

367
00:20:41,280 --> 00:20:44,137
I should probably tell Hulemy
to find somewhere safe to park.

368
00:20:44,220 --> 00:20:46,514
All right, hold on to your butts, guys.

369
00:20:46,880 --> 00:20:48,020
Hey, move it up!

370
00:20:48,500 --> 00:20:49,800
I tried to warn ya.

371
00:20:51,740 --> 00:20:53,440
I knew we'd find them here.

372
00:20:53,600 --> 00:20:56,237
I should've known you'd show
up just in the nick of time.

373
00:20:56,320 --> 00:20:59,217
Hurry, let's move the wounded
inside Voxo's barrier.

374
00:20:59,300 --> 00:21:02,535
If you can still move, carry
somebody who can't inside.

375
00:21:02,640 --> 00:21:04,137
Don't worry, they're the good guys.

376
00:21:04,220 --> 00:21:05,740
You're a lifesaver, Boxo.

377
00:21:06,060 --> 00:21:07,020
You'll be OK.

378
00:21:07,220 --> 00:21:08,737
I'll get you healed up in a jiffy.

379
00:21:08,820 --> 00:21:09,780
Thanks a bunch.

380
00:21:10,700 --> 00:21:11,935
Proceed with caution.

381
00:21:12,040 --> 00:21:13,275
You as well, big sis.

382
00:21:14,360 --> 00:21:15,980
Too hot to handle.

383
00:21:19,580 --> 00:21:20,620
Ding bong!

384
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:24,697
Watching my friends commit acts of
violence reminds me how lucky I am.

385
00:21:24,780 --> 00:21:26,956
They're OP compared to other hunters.

386
00:21:27,640 --> 00:21:30,117
Looks like I don't mean
to bust out my arrows.

387
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:32,537
She's not wrong, but she's also not right.

388
00:21:32,620 --> 00:21:34,738
Time to put that lazy tushy to work.

389
00:21:35,840 --> 00:21:38,740
How do you gotta be so mean, Boxo? Chewy,

390
00:21:39,020 --> 00:21:41,297
didn't I teach you if you
have time to run your mouth,

391
00:21:41,380 --> 00:21:42,637
you have time to pull your weight?

392
00:21:42,720 --> 00:21:44,400
I know, you said it a lot!

393
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:48,020
Huh, is it just me or is
Chewy frightened of something?

394
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:50,421
Eh, I should stop dwelling on it.

395
00:21:51,460 --> 00:21:53,460
Thus, the battle ended in victory.

396
00:21:53,700 --> 00:21:56,457
Thanks to my friends laying the
smack down on those jabronis.

397
00:21:56,540 --> 00:21:59,517
The final battle is almost upon us.

398
00:21:59,600 --> 00:22:02,297
Hey, Boxxo, I could use a drink!

399
00:22:02,380 --> 00:22:04,060
Hello there?

400
00:22:41,820 --> 00:22:47,517
Thank you so

401
00:22:47,600 --> 00:22:48,717
much

402
00:22:48,800 --> 00:22:55,380
for watching.

403
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:37,660
I look forward to serving you again!
